## Quality Check Rules

**All quality verification is done locally. CI is for build confirmation only.**

### Flow

```
Harness-only diff? -> skip quality-check entirely (the gate exempts it;
                      gate-parameter changes are NOT exempt - see Quality Check Hook)
    |
Step 1: Change area + risk level detection (git diff; risk levels per quality policy §1)
    |
Step 2: Build + static checks -> Step 3: tests (High/Medium: cross-check the test-design
        memo). If failures remain after the one fix pass, the cycle ends here (no
        reviewers) and the next cycle starts
    |
Step 4: Review cycle (roster sized by change content - integrated reviewer always,
        falsification QA when code changed, at most one specialist
        (Security > Requirements > Performance); normally 1 cycle; cycles 2+ verify
        fixes with a single verification reviewer)
    |
Step 5: Additional-test proposal (test-recommendation skill: heuristics recommend
        mutation/E2E runs with rationale, the user decides, approved runs execute;
        declines are recorded and never block - except an executed E2E that fails
        must be fixed)
    |
Step 6: Report data saved -> .quality-check-passed (commit-bound JSON) created -> merge allowed
```

Thresholds, cycle caps and time budgets are defined in `documents/development/quality-policy.md` (§1 risk levels, §2 gate matrix, §5 loop protection). Do not restate the numbers here - read them from the policy.

### Quality Check Hook

Codex enforces this via a `PreToolUse` hook (configured in `.codex/hooks.json`). The hook is a static classifier of the command line - it never resolves what actually lands on main; it only stops direct pushes/merges into main (or the trunk equivalent). **The gate stops accidental pushes/merges to main; deliberate evasion is out of scope by design** (enumerated forms live in the hook's own header). **The complete unconditional-block list and fail-open scope live in the `quality-check` skill's "最重要ルール" section (`hook の完全な契約`) - read the full list there, it is not restated here.**

- **Target**: `gh pr merge`, `gh api ...pulls/<n>/merge`, `git merge` / `git pull` / `git rebase` on main or master, a `git push` whose destination refspec matches `main` / `master` exactly, and a `git push` on main or master that omits the refspec or gives only `HEAD` / `@`. **Pushes to feature branches are not gated** by these forms (a line containing a candidate word can still trip an unconditional block - see the skill). `--abort` / `--continue` / `--quit` / `--skip` on `git merge` / `git pull` / `git rebase` are not gated.
- **What passes**: `.quality-check-passed` (commit-bound JSON `{branch, commit}` at the repo root, not consumed) has `commit` equal to (or an abbreviated prefix of) `HEAD` (`branch` is diagnostic only), OR `commit` is an ancestor of `HEAD` and every file in `commit..HEAD` is a harness file with no control-plane touch and no `Quality Gate Overrides` / `mutation_budget_minutes` string change (see the carve-out below - validity is not parsed, a commented-out or fenced change still blocks). Separately, syncing the current trunk from its own remote with no other options - exactly `git pull`, `git pull origin <trunk>`, or `git merge origin/<trunk>` (using the trunk's own name, e.g. the `master` form on a `master` checkout) - needs no flag.
- Harness-only diffs skip the gate and the quality check entirely (`CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.cursorrules`, `.claude/**`, `.codex/**`, `.cursor/**`, `skills/project/**`, `skills/superpowers/**`, `.github/review-*.md`, `documents/development/coding-rules/**`). **Carve-out**: a diff that changes gate parameters - the `Quality Gate Overrides` keys below - is NOT exempt, even inside those paths, and neither is a diff touching **gate control-plane files** (the `quality-check` skill and its schemas, `test-recommendation`, the hook body/registration and its `.codex`/`.cursor` copies, `.claude`/`.codex`/`.cursor` `agents/`/`commands/`/`prompts/`/`rules/` directories, `.codex/config.toml`, the MCP registration files, and `.claude/settings.json` / `.claude/settings.local.json` in their entirety - the full set is defined once in the `quality-check` skill's "ハーネスのみ変更の免除" section). These must go through quality-check; the hook enforces the same carve-out and blocks such diffs with `Gate control-plane changed:`.
- **Trunk names are fixed to `main` / `master`**; products using another trunk name are not gated by the hook and rely on the `permissions.deny` layer and convention.
- **Worktree main** (#116): if the session's working directory is not the worktree, a merge into that worktree's main is invisible to this hook (using `-C` / `cd` is unconditionally blocked though). If the session's working directory is the worktree, that main is gated normally. The hook evaluates in the session's working directory and reads the flag from that repository root (a worktree's own root when the session's working directory is a worktree). The only correct procedure for merging into a `main` checked out in a git worktree is to run quality-check to completion in a session whose working directory is that worktree, creating the flag inside the worktree, then merge from there.
- Candidate operations combined with other commands can still trigger unconditional blocks. A single-line plain `git commit ... && git push [remote]` with omitted refspec is allowed on a feature branch only, without expansion, relocation, redirection or extra commands. Other combinations keep the conservative rule; see the skill for the exact contract.
- If main advanced independently after the flag was issued, the merged main is unverified - re-run quality-check on it before pushing.

